From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alp Lab AB <contact@alplab.ai>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: r9a09g056: make the CPG a syscon

The Renesas RZ remoteproc driver (0020) drives the CM33 reset, clock and
quiesce registers through a CPG regmap (renesas,rz-cpg).  The SYS node is
already a syscon; the CPG node is not, so syscon_regmap_lookup_by_phandle()
fails.  Add "syscon" to its compatible, as the Renesas Multi-OS Package
does.

Opt-in: only applied with ALP_V2N_REMOTEPROC = "1" (linux-renesas bbappend).
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/r9a09g056.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/r9a09g056.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/r9a09g056.dtsi
index e50831b..efe8bae 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/r9a09g056.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/r9a09g056.dtsi
@@ -315,7 +315,7 @@
 		};
 
 		cpg: clock-controller@10420000 {
-			compatible = "renesas,r9a09g056-cpg";
+			compatible = "renesas,r9a09g056-cpg", "syscon";
 			reg = <0 0x10420000 0 0x10000>;
 			clocks = <&audio_extal_clk>, <&audio_clka>,
 				 <&audio_clkb>, <&audio_clkc>,
-- 
